 ## 4. The Options redesign
 
-### 4.1 Pages (7, down from 10)
+### 4.1 Pages (nine tabs: Quick plus eight; built by UI-OPTIONS)
 
-| Page | Short name | Holds (rows) |
+The first plan said seven pages plus Quick and put the Sim page under Game. It does not fit the 12-row rule
+(Game alone would list 19 rows), so the Sim rows are their own **Life** tab. Max 12 rows a page (group headers
+and the page reset row apart; Cheats lists its 12 cheats and the Slider range, 13), at most 3 groups a page.
+A row's page is its `.page` in the option tables (`options.c`, `options_store.c`); its place on the page is the
+layout array in `fp_options.c`. Quick shows copies of its rows (their home page is the other one).
+
+| Page | Tab icon | Groups and rows (in order) |
 |---|---|---|
-| **Game** | Game | Language, Difficulty, Gore, Text speed, Autosave, Tips, Mature, Content notes, Memorial names, Monster Mode, Combat feel, Loss, Pet alerts, News ticker |
-| **Display** | Display | Window skin, Title theme, Cursor, HUD layout, Font style, LCD filter, Camera filter, Clock, Weather, Crosshair + colour, Field of view, Damage numbers, Hit markers, Blood colour, Confetti |
-| **Sound** | Sound | Music, Sound, Voice volume (slider rows with a live preview note), Voice babble, Subtitles |
-| **Controls** | Controls | Control scheme, Turn buttons, Stick mode (Dreamcast one-stick), Invert look, Look speed, Aim assist, Lock-on, Camera, Shoulder, Rumble |
-| **Access** | Access | Screen shake, Head bob, Reduce flashes, Colourblind aid, UI bounce, Font style (shared link), Subtitles (shared link) |
-| **Perf** | Perf | Combat detail, Effects detail, Draw distance (PS1 3D), Show FPS, Demon density |
-| **Cheats** | Cheats | the 12 cheats and Slider range (locked ones show "???" and their hint as today) |
-
-Quick stays as the front **Quick** page (Language, volumes, Text speed, Difficulty, Gore, Preset), so the
-tab strip is Quick plus the seven above = 8 short names (4-5 letters each, icons at 240x160). The Sim page
-(Possessions, Town events, Sim speed, Day length) joins **Game** under a "Life" sub-group header row; the
-Shooter page's rows are spread over Display (looks), Controls (aim) and Perf (Demon density) as listed.
-Row ids and the option store do not change (OPT / OPT2 stay loadable): only `.page` in the info tables and the
-row order move; `doomo_option_page_names` and the page enum change in step (add-only is kept for saved page
-indices: the page is never saved).
+| **Quick** | bolt | Language, Music volume, Sound volume, Text speed, Difficulty, Gore, Preset |
+| **Game** | heart | *Play:* Language, Difficulty, Gore, Combat feel, Text speed, Autosave. *Content:* Mature, Content notes, Memorial names, Monster Mode. *Help:* Tips, Show all tips again |
+| **Life** | house | *Time:* Sim speed, Day length. *Island:* Possessions, Town events, Weather, News ticker. *Care:* Pet alerts, Loss |
+| **Display** | spark | *Look:* Window skin, Title theme, Cursor, Clock, LCD filter. *View:* Camera filter, HUD layout, Crosshair, Crosshair colour, Field of view. *Splatter:* Blood colour, Confetti |
+| **Sound** | note | Music volume, Sound volume, Voice volume, Voice babble |
+| **Controls** | A cap | *Pad:* Control scheme, Turn buttons, Stick mode (a one-stick Dreamcast pad), Rumble (where there is a motor). *Camera:* Camera, Shoulder, Invert look, Look speed. *Aim:* Aim assist, Lock-on, Damage numbers, Hit markers |
+| **Access** | smile | *Read:* Font style, Subtitles, Colourblind aid. *Calm:* Reduce flashes, Screen shake, Head bob, UI bounce |
+| **Perf** | cloud | Combat detail, Effects detail, Draw distance (PS1 3D), Show FPS, Demon density |
+| **Cheats** | skull | the 12 cheats and Slider range (locked ones show "???" and their hint as today) |
+
+Row ids and the option store do not change (OPT / OPT2 stay loadable): only `.page` and the row order moved.
+`OPTPAGE_AUDIO` and `OPTPAGE_SIM` stay as aliases of `OPTPAGE_SOUND` and `OPTPAGE_LIFE`; `OPTPAGE_SHOOTER` is gone
+(its rows are on Display, Controls, Access, Perf and Game). The page is never saved. A preset still never
+touches the Perf rows (3D detail, effects, draw distance, FPS); Demon density moved to Perf as a row but a
+preset may still set it (it is a game setting). Weather went to Life, Subtitles and Font style to Access (one
+page each: no shared links).
 
